{"question": "How does the index endpoint call repository indexing?", "expected_paths": ["src/repoguide/main.py", "src/repoguide/indexer.py"], "answer": "Based on the provided repository evidence, the index endpoint (`index_repo` in `src/repoguide/main.py`) calls repository indexing through the following steps:\n\n1. It receives an `IndexRepositoryRequest` and a database session (`SessionDep`) [S2].\n2. It validates the GitHub URL by calling `parse_github_url(str(request.url))` [S2, S7].\n3. It calls the `index_repository` function, passing the string version of the request URL and the session [S2]:\n   ```python\n   repo = index_repository(\n       str(request.url),\n       session,\n   )\n   ```", "sources": [{"label": "S1", "file_path": "src/repoguide/indexer.py", "symbol_name": "index_repository", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 78, "distance": 0.6170220260924704, "origin": "hybrid", "channels": ["dense", "keyword"], "fusion_score": 0.03200204813108039, "rerank_score": 0.39067673683166504}, {"label": "S2", "file_path": "src/repoguide/main.py", "symbol_name": "index_repo", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 65, "distance": 0.5989902972573219, "origin": "hybrid", "channels": ["dense", "keyword"], "fusion_score": 0.02921395544346364, "rerank_score": -0.523982048034668}, {"label": "S3", "file_path": "src/repoguide/indexer.py", "symbol_name": null, "start_line": 56, "end_line": 115, "distance": 0.75232675685446, "origin": "hybrid", "channels": ["dense", "keyword"], "fusion_score": 0.025807525807525808, "rerank_score": -1.2213435173034668}, {"label": "S4", "file_path": "src/repoguide/indexer.py", "symbol_name": null, "start_line": 111, "end_line": 118, "distance": 0.6099446067164485, "origin": "hybrid", "channels": ["dense"], "fusion_score": 0.016129032258064516, "rerank_score": -2.694704294204712}, {"label": "S5", "file_path": "src/repoguide/main.py", "symbol_name": "ask_repository", "start_line": 94, "end_line": 127, "distance": 0.6550014121830029, "origin": "hybrid", "cha