{"question": "How does the ask endpoint reach generation?", "expected_paths": ["src/repoguide/main.py", "src/repoguide/rag.py", "src/repoguide/llm.py"], "answer": "Based on the provided repository evidence, the `/repositories/{repo_id}/ask` endpoint reaches text generation through the following flow:\n\n1. **Endpoint Trigger (`ask_repository`)**: \n   When a POST request is made to `/repositories/{repo_id}/ask`, the `ask_repository` function in `src/repoguide/main.py` validates that the repository exists and that its status is `\"indexed\"` [S1]. If valid, it calls `answer_question` [S1].\n\n2. **RAG & Retrieval (`answer_question`)**:\n   The `answer_question` function in `src/repoguide/rag.py` handles the retrieval mode (either `\"graph\"` or `\"dense\"`) to fetch relevant code hits [S4]. \n   - If `retrieval_mode` is `\"graph\"`, it calls `retrieve_with_graph` [S4].\n   - If `retrieval_mode` is `\"dense\"`, it calls `retrieve` [S4].\n   \n   If no hits are found, it returns a default message (\"No indexed code was available.\") [S4]. Otherwise, it formats the retrieved chunks into a context string and constructs a prompt containing the untrusted repository evidence, instructions, and the user's question [S4].\n\n3. **Generation (`generate_answer`)**:\n   Finally, `answer_question` passes the constructed prompt to `generate_answer(prompt)` and returns the resulting answer along with the sources [S4].", "sources": [{"label": "S1", "file_path": "src/repoguide/main.py", "symbol_name": "ask_repository", "start_line": 94, "end_line": 127, "distance": 0.7927421305929341, "origin": "hybrid", "channels": ["dense", "keyword"], "fusion_score": 0.03252247488101534, "rerank_score": -9.557562828063965}, {"label": "S2", "file_path": "src/repoguide/intelligence.py", "symbol_name": "last_line", "start_line": 86, "end_line": 88, "distance": 0.8602046304819205, "origin": "hybrid", "channels": ["dense"], "fusion_score": 0.013333333333333334, "rerank_score": -10.111122131347656}, {"la